  {
   "id": 2,
   "ref": "565–570",
   "en": "Won't you flee from here headlong, while flight is still possible? Soon you will see the sea churned up with ships, and fierce torches blazing, soon the shore ablaze with fire — if dawn finds you still lingering in this land. [Come now|27,28], break off your delay. A woman is always a changeable, unpredictable thing.' [With those words|36,37] [he vanished into|39,40] the black night.",
   "en_marked": "[Won't|1] [you flee|2] [from here|3] [headlong|4], [while|5] [flight|6] is {still|Added for urgency: dum praecipitare potestas means while you have the power, and still implies the chance will soon be gone.} [possible|7]? [Soon|8] [you will see|13] the [sea|9] [churned up|10] with [ships|11], [and|12] [fierce|12] [torches|15] [blazing|14], [soon|16] the [shore|18] [ablaze|17] with [fire|19] — [if|20] [dawn|25] [finds|23] [you|21] still [lingering|26] in [this|22] [land|24]. [Come now|27,28], [break off|29] your [delay|30]. A [woman|35] {is|Supplied: the Latin leaves out est, as it often does in short sayings.} [always|34] a [changeable|31], [unpredictable|33] {thing|Added to show that varium et mutabile are neuter: a woman is a fickle and changeable thing.}.' [With those words|36,37] [he vanished into|39,40] the [black|41] [night|38].",
