  {
   "id": 3,
   "ref": "571–579",
   "en": "Then indeed Aeneas, terrified by the sudden vision, tore himself from sleep and roused his men, urgent: 'Wake up, men, quickly — take your places at the oars; loose the sails, and hurry. A god sent down from high heaven — look — is spurring us on again, to hasten our flight and cut the twisted ropes. We follow you, whoever you are, one of the blessed gods, and joyfully obey your command once more. Be with us, come gently to our aid, and set kind stars in the sky above us.'",
   "en_marked": "[Then|1] [indeed|2] [Aeneas|3], [terrified|5] by the [sudden|4] [vision|6], [tore|7] [himself|10] [from|8] [sleep|9] [and|11] [roused|12] his [men|11], [urgent|13]: '[Wake up|14], [men|15], [quickly|21] — [take your places|17] [at the oars|18]; [loose|19] the [sails|20], and [hurry|21]. [A god|22] [sent down|24] [from|25] [high|26] [heaven|23] — [look|32] — [is spurring us on|34] [again|33], [to hasten|27] our [flight|28] [and|29] [cut|30] the [twisted|29] [ropes|31]. [We follow|35] [you|36], [whoever|39] [you are|40], one of the [blessed|37] [gods|38], [and|41] [joyfully|44] [obey|43] your [command|41] [once more|42]. [Be with us|45], [come|48] [gently|47] [to our aid|48], [and|49] [set|53] [kind|52] [stars|50] [in the sky|51] {above us|Added for clarity; caelo alone means in the sky.}.'",
